{"title":"Ellipse Proof Problem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ellipse_Proof_Problem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/9/e69ad33a4a598a35596905edc647cbc22f929bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(u,v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" /> be a point on the ellipse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d345c8f937303d30bfe28aa69145801b62f60b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^2}{a^2}+\\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1\\;(a&gt;b&gt;0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"194\" height=\"41\" />. The two tangents of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e60dcda5bc7e8522223ab86d2ad74c3749844e5b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-x_0)^2+(y-y_0)^2=r^2\\quad (0&lt;r&lt;b, (x_0-u)(y_0-v)\\neq 0)\\]\" width=\"474\" height=\"20\" />\nthrough <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> are drawn, intersecting the ellipse at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f87e235a36d533fd186185dfe675b1968f54eaf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" />. Prove that the line containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> passes through a fixed point as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> varies.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ellipse_Proof_Problem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the equation of the tangent line be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/0/b007c6ea60c11b064fa819f6889dfb55c78700b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=k(x-u)+v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50d12d1a8291122eec5ee92675182db3e40ef5fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kx-y-ku+v=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />. The distance between the centre of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and the tangent line is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. By the point-to-line distance formula, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/a/45a5733b45cc08dd4a48ca6987bb4a4ed7d0de2e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\lvert kx_0-y_0-ku+v\\rvert}{\\sqrt{k^2+1}}=r\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"43\" />\nSquaring the above equation, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f039ef13f6a77300b84bfe34c922cb62cf201e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^2(k^2+1)=(x_0-u)^2k^2-2(x_0-u)(y_0-v)k+(y_0-v)^2\\]\" width=\"451\" height=\"20\" />\nRearranging,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/b/14b75cfc728716340bae3a28b32c3a0a2702ad48.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\bigl((x_0-u)^2-r^2\\bigr)k^2-2(x_0-u)(y_0-v)k+(y_0-v)^2-r^2=0\\]\" width=\"473\" height=\"21\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/6/ca6f60cce1189a82b6be3e48d236afedb2b2850e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1,k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> be the slopes of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/5/e956bb95054645df67798a7d96dbb4556f129920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB,AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" />, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/8/3383d428a4355b3185a868d45501f599666cb44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X=(x_0-u),Y=(y_0-v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"216\" height=\"20\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/2/0529428fe2c477b676dad411db9327b50286a80c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=k_1+k_2,P=k_1k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" />. By Vieta's Formula,\n\\begin{align*}\nS=\\frac{2XY}{X^2-r^2},\\quad P=\\frac{Y^2-r^2}{X^2-r^2}\\tag{*}\n\\end{align*}\nBy the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ellipse#Equation_of_Chord_Using_Weierstrass_Substitution\" title=\"Ellipse\">Weierstrass substitution</a>, we approach the problem using the parameterized coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a5aaa74de5f3fe32c27d34c7e552c23ee6a25c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(t_1),B(t_2),C(t_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/0/730db30a117a16de72cbf3703048fb3d5168639b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1=\\frac{b}{a}\\cdot\\frac{t_1t_2-1}{t_1+t_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"133\" height=\"42\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a40dccc3bb61d55c03b7dafe15707eeef43885ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c429de80a5a0492b66cca5e5b2ecca5875a475e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_2=\\frac{ak_1t_1+b}{bt_1-ak_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"115\" height=\"42\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa0b391f60e2370f422a15c5b1c3220f0ecd6d55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_3=\\frac{ak_2t_1+b}{bt_1-ak_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"115\" height=\"42\" />. The equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> can be written using parameters:\n\\begin{align*}\nay(t_2+t_3)-bx(t_2t_3-1)=ab(t_2t_3+1)\\tag{1}\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Evaluating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/8/e487584201ac372a8a06922381796524eadcae07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_2+t_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />:\n\\begin{align*}\nt_2+t_3&amp;=\\frac{\\sum_{cyc}abt_1^2k_1+b^2t_1-a^2t_1k_1k_2-abk_2}{b^2t_1^2-abt_1k_1-abt_1k_2+a^2k_1k_2}\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{abt_1^2S+2b^2t_1-2a^2t_1P-abS}{b^2t_1^2-abt_1S+a^2P}\n\\end{align*}\nEvaluating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/0/650b020efde804b48df2e52d72a985e61cf562a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_2t_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />:\n\\begin{align*}\nt_2t_3&amp;=\\frac{ak_1t_1+b}{bt_1-ak_1}\\cdot\\frac{ak_2t_1+b}{bt_1-ak_2}\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{a^2t_1^2k_1k_2+abt_1k_2+abt_1k_1+b^2}{b^2t_1^2-abt_1S+a^2P}\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{a^2t_1^2P+abt_1S+b^2}{b^2t_1^2-abt_1S+a^2P}\n\\end{align*}\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/d/cfdc6949c457c697486bf84b4f1ba030b6e7a485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_2+t_3=\\frac{N_1}{D_e},t_2t_3=\\frac{N_2}{D_e}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"189\" height=\"42\" />. We multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6cabed0e2acac9025ecfee63ff0ec20d81ef1dff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> to eliminate the common denominator <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6cabed0e2acac9025ecfee63ff0ec20d81ef1dff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> from both sides:\n\\begin{align*}\nay\\cdot N_1-bx(N_2-D_e)=ab(N_2+D_e)\\tag{2}\n\\end{align*}\nWe have\n\\begin{align*}\nN_1&amp;=abt_1^2S+2b^2t_1-2a^2t_1P-abS\\\\\nN_2-D_e&amp;=a^2t_1^2P-b^2t_1^2+2abt_1S+b^2-a^2P\\\\\nN_2+D_e&amp;=a^2t_1^2P+b^2t_1^2+a^2P+b^2\n\\end{align*}\nWhile substituting the above expressions into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, we group them by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85bdb8aade47b0108d4aa45e54451c244ed67ee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S,P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />:\n\\begin{align*}\nS(a^2b(t_1^2-1)y-2ab^2t_1x)+P(-2a^3t_1y-a^2b(t_1^2-1)x-a^3b(t_1^2+1))=-2ab^2t_1y-b^3(t_1^2-1)x+ab^3(t_1^2+1)\\tag{3}\n\\end{align*}\nLet\n\\begin{gather*}\nc_1=a^2b(t_1^2-1),\\quad c_2=2ab^2t_1,\\quad c_3=2a^3t_1,\\\\\nc_4=a^2b(t_1^2-1),\\quad c_5=a^3b(t_1^2+1),\\quad c_6=2ab^2t_1,\\\\\nc_7=b^3(t_1^2-1),\\quad c_8=ab^3(t_1^2+1)\n\\end{gather*}\nRecall from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d02e715e7f7195675151570530c5b62ba7b2744.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(*)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> that the common denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85bdb8aade47b0108d4aa45e54451c244ed67ee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S,P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/58293be12c8907597c525877260e90f286d1e096.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X^2-r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />. Multiplying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/58293be12c8907597c525877260e90f286d1e096.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X^2-r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/9/3f97af55a33d139c837ac33dcb0e4a0765893367.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2XY(c_1y-c_2x)+(Y^2-r^2)(-c_3y-c_4x-c_5)=(X^2-r^2)(-c_6y-c_7x+c_8)\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"20\" />\nRegrouping the terms by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e2221c84f16a3f75ae07e5023384cc40d9c05357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/4/0543dafa1da256ec5cd7390a592757a64e6f0a78.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^2\\bigl((c_3-c_6)y+(c_4-c_7)x+(c_5+c_8)\\bigr)=(-2c_1XY+c_3Y^2-c_6X^2)y+(2c_2XY+c_4Y^2-c_7X^2)x+c_5Y^2+c_8X^2\\]\" width=\"782\" height=\"21\" />\nNote that a coordinate that always satisfies this parametric (with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />) equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/817278636cbacfe099397cd00ef69da7627f2bc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2F(x,y)=G(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"21\" /> is the solution to the system\n\\begin{align*}\nF(x,y)=0\\\\\nG(x,y)=0\n\\end{align*}\nWe rewrite the system as \n\\begin{align*}\nA_1y+B_1x=C_1\\\\\nA_2y+B_2x=C_2,\n\\end{align*}\nwhere\n\\begin{align*}\nA_1&amp;=c_3-c_6=2a(a^2-b^2)t_1\\\\\nB_1&amp;=c_4-c_7=b(a^2-b^2)(t_1^2-1)\\\\\nC_1&amp;=-c_5-c_8=-ab(a^2+b^2)(t_1^2+1)\\\\\nA_2&amp;=-2a^2b(t_1^2-1)XY+2a^3t_1Y^2-2ab^2t_1X^2\\\\\nB_2&amp;=4ab^2t_1XY+a^2b(t_1^2-1)Y^2-b^3(t_1^2-1)X^2\\\\\nC_2&amp;=-a^3b(t_1^2+1)Y^2-ab^3(t_1^2+1)X^2\n\\end{align*}\nRecall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bf224349705aaf35cfff4d7af5cf6d6dc545351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=a\\cdot\\frac{1-t_1^2}{1+t_1^2},v=b\\cdot\\frac{2t_1}{1+t_1^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"221\" height=\"45\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/9156f9eac25c82bcfbeb89a4dae0174b882d2900.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1^2=\\frac{a-u}{a+u}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"86\" height=\"39\" />, and substituting this into the second equation gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/7/147df209fa8f524a01a89d391f01071802352bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1=\\frac{av}{(a+u)b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"108\" height=\"39\" />. Along with the conditions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d879cb159685457b91c52f3053b06cc1d9dc0c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1^2-1=\\frac{-2u}{a+u}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"118\" height=\"40\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/8/2c8ff2688b8b85c2e61815d93ce1602d53dff507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1^2+1=\\frac{2a}{a+u}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"118\" height=\"40\" />, we rewrite the 6 coefficients:\n\\begin{align*}\nA_1&amp;=\\frac{2a^2v(a^2-b^2)}{(a+u)b}\\\\\nB_1&amp;=\\frac{-2bu(a^2-b^2)}{a+u}\\\\\nC_1&amp;=\\frac{-2a^2b(a^2+b^2)}{a+u}\\\\\nA_2&amp;=\\frac{2a^2}{a+u}\\left(2buXY+\\frac{a^2v}{b}Y^2-bvX^2\\right)\\\\\nB_2&amp;=\\frac{2bu}{a+u}\\left(\\frac{2a^2v}{u}XY-a^2Y^2+b^2X^2\\right)\\\\\nC_2&amp;=\\frac{-2a^2b}{a+u}(a^2Y^2+b^2X^2)\n\\end{align*}\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/e/8ee7bfb016fe0d199887d9635a1e6bcd39cb2dcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2=\\frac{2a^2}{a+u}A_2&#39;,\\quad B_2=\\frac{2bu}{a+u}B_2&#39;,\\quad C_2=\\frac{-2a^2b}{a+u}C_2&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"394\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p>Evaluating the determinant of the system <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73a96669a680999fd2d4acee3f1e9461375d8c5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1B_2-A_2B_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" />:\n\\begin{align*}\nA_1B_2-A_2B_1&amp;=\\frac{2a^2v(a^2-b^2)}{(a+u)b}\\cdot \\frac{2bu}{a+u}B_2'-\\frac{2a^2}{a+u}A_2'\\cdot \\frac{-2bu(a^2-b^2)}{a+u}\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{4a^2uv(a^2-b^2)}{(a+u)^2}B_2'+\\frac{4a^2bu(a^2-b^2)}{(a+u)^2}A_2'\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{4a^2uv(a^2-b^2)}{(a+u)^2}(B_2'+\\frac{b}{v}A_2')\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{4a^2uv(a^2-b^2)}{(a+u)^2}XY\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2a^2v}{u}+\\frac{2b^2u}{v}\\right)\n\\end{align*}\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is on the ellipse, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/3/7a35f92da359ef4b7b2d6a39fc9eac67a9f44613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2u^2+a^2v^2=a^2b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c5344f38b57c1d32c869718b7f516fb32aa9428b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2a^2v}{u}+\\frac{2b^2u}{v}=\\frac{2}{uv}(a^2v^2+b^2u^2)=\\frac{2a^2b^2}{uv}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"324\" height=\"41\" />. It follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e4c50ce1e23b02d860727c658f9a417df45c158.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_1B_2-A_2B_1=\\frac{8a^4b^2(a^2-b^2)}{(a+u)^2}XY\\]\" width=\"275\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>We proceed by computing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Evaluating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/7/c7762464a5705b5fe95dfba9633667d9fd2fb751.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1C_2-A_2C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" />:\n\\begin{align*}\nA_1C_2-A_2C_1&amp;=\\frac{2a^2v(a^2-b^2)}{(a+u)b}\\cdot \\frac{-2a^2b}{a+u}C_2'-\\frac{2a^2}{a+u}A_2'\\cdot \\frac{-2a^2b(a^2+b^2)}{a+u}\\\\\n&amp;=-\\frac{4a^4v(a^2-b^2)}{(a+u)^2}C_2'+\\frac{4a^4b(a^2+b^2)}{(a+u)^2}A_2'\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{4a^4}{(a+u)^2}(-v(a^2-b^2)C_2'+b(a^2+b^2)A_2')\n\\end{align*}\nGrouping the coefficients by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/943ce8b6352fc0fc65e2baa25a7de7706ac1b7ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY,Y^2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0872ca2f62e98f7846c7ed24f6953417c2643dbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X^2$\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" />, we have\n\\begin{align*}\nA_1C_2-A_2C_1&amp;=\\frac{4a^4}{(a+u)^2}(2b^2u(a^2+b^2)XY+2a^2b^2v(Y^2-X^2))\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{8a^4b^2}{(a+u)^2}(a^2v(Y^2-X^2)+u(a^2+b^2)XY)\n\\end{align*}\nThus, we have the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-coordinate of our desired point:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c678485702f7479041baf539569bcaeab5e48609.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\gamma_x=\\frac{A_1C_2-A_2C_1}{A_1B_2-A_2B_1}=\\frac{a^2v(Y^2-X^2)+u(a^2+b^2)XY}{(a^2-b^2)XY}\\]\" width=\"420\" height=\"44\" />\nEvaluating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b102b08ad5ac5b765cc6a4b908f06f78d1cf539.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_2C_1-B_1C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" /> similarly:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/0/3a003c75065486766ff9e22ae8fcb2643d30e110.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[B_2C_1-B_1C_2=\\frac{8a^4b^2}{(a+u)^2}(b^2u(Y^2-X^2)-v(a^2+b^2)XY)\\]\" width=\"449\" height=\"44\" />\nThus, we have the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate of our desired point:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a924661d3ed51ccac5c0f98d6fce9f94a301dc29.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\gamma_y=\\frac{B_2C_1-B_1C_2}{A_1B_2-A_2B_1}=\\frac{b^2u(Y^2-X^2)-v(a^2+b^2)XY}{(a^2-b^2)XY}\\]\" width=\"418\" height=\"44\" />\nTherefore, by our initial definition for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/c/81cee936d2982eea5fb6e68b6167da70a1c690fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X,Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" />, we have the point with coordinates\n\\begin{gather*}\n\\gamma_x=\\frac{a^2v(y_0+x_0-u-v)(y_0-x_0+u-v)+u(a^2+b^2)(x_0-u)(y_0-v)}{(a^2-b^2)(x_0-u)(y_0-v)}\\\\\n\\gamma_y=\\frac{b^2u(y_0+x_0-u-v)(y_0-x_0+u-v)-v(a^2+b^2)(x_0-u)(y_0-v)}{(a^2-b^2)(x_0-u)(y_0-v)}\n\\end{gather*}\nthat would consistently lie on the line containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, which is fixed regardless of the choice of a valid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, as desired.\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ellipse_Proof_Problem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Conic_section\" title=\"Conic section\">Conic sections</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ellipse\" title=\"Ellipse\">Ellipse</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">Geometry</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomial\" title=\"Polynomial\">Polynomials</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cramer%27s_Rule\" title=\"Cramer&#39;s Rule\">Cramer's Rule</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018083415\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 345/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 12660/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37844:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018083415 and revision id 292492. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}